ld: arm Linux: link executables at the RP2350 ATRANS window by default

ATRANS programs on native RP2350 Linux are static ELFs whose segments lie in
[0x11000000, 0x11400000), with the stack below the lowest segment. The
default is 0x11020000 (128 KiB of stack); -Wl,-Ttext-segment=ADDR overrides.

--- a/ld/emulparams/armelf_linux.sh
+++ b/ld/emulparams/armelf_linux.sh
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 OTHER_END_SYMBOLS="${CREATE_SHLIB+PROVIDE (}__end__ = .${CREATE_SHLIB+)};"
 OTHER_SECTIONS='.note.gnu.arm.ident 0 : { KEEP (*(.note.gnu.arm.ident)) }'
 
-TEXT_START_ADDR=0x00010000
+TEXT_START_ADDR=0x11020000
 TARGET2_TYPE=got-rel
 
 # ARM does not support .s* sections.
